GUI: keep pop-up lists open after a slow tap on touchscreens

A pop-up list closes and picks the item under the pointer when the button
is released more than 300 ms after it opened. On a touchscreen that is a
tap, not a drag, and on slow (e-ink) screens taps take longer than that:
the list opened and closed again on its own. With kFeatureTouchscreen an
unmoved release always keeps the list open.

--- a/gui/widgets/popup.cpp
+++ b/gui/widgets/popup.cpp
@@ -160,7 +160,10 @@
 	// Mouse was released. If it wasn't moved much since the original mouse down,
 	// let the popup stay open. If it did move, assume the user made his selection.
 	int dist = (_clickX - absX) * (_clickX - absX) + (_clickY - absY) * (_clickY - absY);
-	if (dist > 3 * 3 || g_system->getMillis() - _openTime > 300) {
+	// On a touchscreen a tap is never a drag: lifting the finger where it went
+	// down keeps the list open however long the tap took (slow screens).
+	bool slowRelease = g_system->getMillis() - _openTime > 300 && !g_system->hasFeature(OSystem::kFeatureTouchscreen);
+	if (dist > 3 * 3 || slowRelease) {
 		int item = findItem(x, y);
 
 		// treat separator item as if no item was clicked
